# Redis 7 ACL file for VPS-1. Render it, never copy it: `deploy.sh` fills the two placeholders from
# /srv/madar/.env into /srv/madar/redis/users.acl (mode 640, group 999, in a 750 directory) before
# Compose starts Redis. Real passwords never enter the repository (constitution V, FR-052).
#
# Two users:
#   default — api-admin, api-public, the workers and the healthcheck, over the VCN and wg0.
#   homebox — the owner's x86-64 scrape box, which reaches only Redis on wg0 (research R21). Its
#             patterns cover what it uses: Celery's prefixed keys and channels, the token buckets
#             and its fetch locks. The control channel is `&celery:/0.celery.pidbox`: a worker
#             PSUBSCRIBEs it, and Redis matches a pattern literally, so `&celery:*` alone is not
#             enough and the worker exits with NoPermissionError (B2-R2-3). `+@write` grants SADD,
#             so a set is possible; `-@dangerous` and `-@admin` keep it out of CONFIG, FLUSHALL and
#             KEYS. Narrowed on D2 from a real worker run, `tests/adapters/test_homebox_acl.py`.
user default on >${REDIS_PASSWORD} ~* &* +@all
user homebox on >${REDIS_HOMEBOX_PASSWORD} ~celery:* ~ratelimit:* ~lock:fetch:* &celery:* &celery:/0.celery.pidbox -@all +@connection +@read +@write +@keyspace +@string +@list +@hash +@sortedset +@transaction +@scripting +@pubsub -@admin -@dangerous
